| 434 | `Number`'s `=` between a float and an exact number compares after `asFloat`, so it calls unequal values equal and is not transitive: `1/3 = asFloat(1/3)` is `true`, and so is `((widen(1) LSHIFT 60) + widen(1)) = asFloat(widen(1) LSHIFT 60)` | NEGATIVE-VERIFIED | design limit (library) | silent | none | climb batch 6 rung F's skeptic | `Number`'s one `opr =` (`Library/FortressLibrary.fss:386-392` at c124c6b65) compares a pair with an `RR64` or `RR32` side by `asFloat(self) = asFloat(other)` and two exact numbers as rationals; its doc comment (`:383-385`) states the rule. Comparing a float by its exact rational value is transitive but needs a float-to-rational conversion the library lacks (the curator's choice). The specification compares only a rational with a rational (`Specification/basic-lib/numbers.tex`, "Rational Numbers"). Probe `explorations/compile-ladder/rung-flat-tower/probes/skeptic/sk-exprs-equality.txt:19-26`, in the parent of ab067d9b6; full text: history, row 434 |
